{
 "answer": {
  "answer": "The goal was not met. Repeats confirmed only two of the five challenging cases the brief asked for, each on a different scene: 096988dd with the car at its recorded timing and speed and the ego at 1.4x (S13), and 19f339ba with the car as recorded and the ego at 1.2x (S43). In both, the trigger was the faster ego at hand-off, not the retimed car. Every failure was the policy's fault and none looks like a simulator artifact: the ego braked or slowed, drifted left out of its lane and hit a car driving alongside in the next lane, which was never the car the study retimed. A third setting on 096988dd (S12: car 1 s earlier and 1.5x, ego 1.2x) failed every time, but it shares a scene with S13 and has only two runs, so it is a strong hint rather than a separate case. The 90% ranges for the two confirmed settings only just clear 0.5, and no other scene produced a failure in the budget.",
  "findings": [
   {
    "claim": "On 096988dd, raising only the ego's speed at hand-off to 1.4x (car at recorded timing and speed) made the policy fail on every repeat. Each time it slowed and angled left, and its front-left corner hit actor 41 in the left lane while the lead truck stayed well ahead. This is a confirmed case, with the policy at fault.",
    "settings": [
     "S13"
    ]
   },
   {
    "claim": "On 19f339ba, raising only the ego's speed to 1.2x (car as recorded) made the policy fail on every repeat. It braked hard with no close lead, its path bent left, and it clipped actor 1 in the left lane. Getting rear-ended came after the hard braking and is not what made these failures. This is a confirmed case, with the policy at fault.",
    "settings": [
     "S43"
    ]
   },
   {
    "claim": "On 096988dd, also moving the car 1 s earlier at 1.5x with the ego at 1.2x failed in both runs, in the same way: a left drift into actor 41. This suggests that on this scene the faster ego does the work and the car's retiming does not matter, but two runs are not a confirmed rate.",
    "settings": [
     "S12",
     "S13"
    ]
   },
   {
    "claim": "The same ego-only change (car as recorded, ego at 1.4x) did not fail on the other scenes tried. Each of those settings has a single run, so this is only a hint that the left-drift failure belongs to the scene.",
    "settings": [
     "S9",
     "S17",
     "S24",
     "S25",
     "S29",
     "S33",
     "S41"
    ]
   },
   {
    "claim": "The two settings repeated most without a failure were near misses with a slowed car and a fast ego: 023b7fcc with the car at 0.75x and the ego at 1.4x, and 12855a41 with the car at 0.5x and the ego at 1.4x. Their failure rates are bounded well below 0.5, so these are near misses, not failure cases.",
    "settings": [
